From 7eac5ea5bff5893c7097fbe01dfa9ea87a32fac6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Wed, 20 May 2026 09:36:52 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] perf phase 11 patch 0163 -- engine data cache (486-campaign
 Bug 1 structural fix)

486-campaign Bug 1 -- the stage-load freeze with audio cutout on
DX2-66. flush-instr #93 sec.18 verdict: Leg A v2's audio mid-gap
pump was structurally insufficient -- a single uninterruptible fread
on a .pbm tileset (~64-100 KB, ~400-1400 ms on CompactFlash) exceeds
the audio ring depth (~372 ms), so no in-engine pump can bridge a
single fread. The cache approach eliminates the disk wait at the
source by preloading .pbm bitmap assets into RAM at boot and
intercepting Surface::loadImage to consume the cached blob.

Cached read at ~5-20 ms < 372 ms ring depth -> the ring does not
underrun during stage loads -> the audible freeze goes away.

v2 (revise vs v1 -- build-qa #94 link gate caught funopen + fmemopen
both absent from DJGPP libc; revise drops the myfopen intercept
entirely): scope narrowed to .pbm files only. All .pbm reads in the
engine route through Surface::loadImage -> SDL_LoadBMP, so a single
intercept point (Intercept B) covers the dominant freeze cause
(Tileset::load .pbm reads). The other small engine assets
(.pxm / .pxe / .pxa / .tsc / .pxt routed via fopen/myfopen) are NOT
cached: each individual fread is sub-ring-depth so they do not
cause audible underrun on their own. v2 scoping; v3 may widen if
iter shows residual misses.

v2 cache scope: Stage/*.pbm (tilesets, the dominant freeze cause) +
Npc/*.pbm (NPC sprite sheets) + top-level *.pbm (UI/HUD: Face*,
Arms, Bullet, Caret, casts, ArmImg, ...), ~2.6 MB total, ~5-10 s
additional boot wall-clock on CF. The operator's machine (48 MB RAM,
~30 MB free heap) has ample headroom for the v2 budget.

Single interception point -- Surface::loadImage in
graphics/Surface.cpp. This is the surgical fix for Tileset::load's
.pbm path (the dominant freeze cause). Surface::loadImage was using
SDL_LoadBMP directly (NOT IMG_Load -- verified against source; the
two IMG_Load sites in src/ are Font.cpp's font atlas PNG and
Renderer.cpp's spotlight PNG, both one-time at boot, not on the
freeze critical path -- v2 leaves them alone). The intercept checks
the cache by absolute path; on hit, uses SDL_LoadBMP_IO on an
SDL_IOFromConstMem-backed SDL_IOStream; on miss or with cache
disabled, falls through to plain SDL_LoadBMP. The post-load
colorkey + INDEX8 + paletteRemap path is byte-source-agnostic
(operates on the resulting SDL_Surface), so colorkey handling is
byte-identical between the two paths -- the cache only changes
WHERE the bytes come from.

SDL_LoadBMP_IO + SDL_IOFromConstMem are SDL3-provided -- no libc
dependency, which is why v2 sidesteps the v1 link failure
(funopen + fmemopen both absent from DJGPP).

Killswitch: SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_DATA_CACHE. v2 default OFF (opt-in
via "=1"). Same hygiene as nxengine/0162-v2 -- ship opt-in; flip to
default-ON in a release patch after iter validation confirms
freeze elimination + no memory issues + no broken-render-frame
regressions. Sentinel-cached on first nxe::cache::enabled() call --
single SDL_GetHint then cached int; banner emit
"data cache: ENABLED (opt-in)" / "data cache: DISABLED (default)"
on the decision.

Boot-time preload in nxe::cache::init(), called from main.cpp right
after SDL_Init (SDL_GetHint needs SDL_Init; Logger needs to be up
for LOG_INFO; this precedes settings_load / Renderer init / Sound
init). Preload order is access-pattern: Stage -> Npc -> top-level
.pbm. The highest-stakes asset class (Stage/ -- the dominant freeze
cause) loads first so the operator's first stage transition is
RAM-fast even if a later phase is interrupted (e.g. malloc failure
descopes top-level but Stage/ is already resident).

Defensive fallbacks (per the #94 STOP-and-ack):
- D1 cache-miss fallback: Surface::loadImage falls through to
  plain SDL_LoadBMP if the blob is not found OR cache is disabled.
  Modded assets, optional files, and the cache-disabled path all
  use stdio.
- D2 malloc-failure resilience: per-file try-allocate; on NULL the
  file is skipped + logged + preload continues. Partial cache is
  still better than none; the lookup miss falls through to disk
  (D1). Final log line at preload end reports
  "N files / M bytes resident / S skipped (X bytes malloc-failed)".
- D3 no eviction in v2: everything preloaded stays resident for the
  process lifetime. Defer LRU / budget cap until iter surfaces a
  need.

CACHE-OFF path (the v2 default): byte-identical rendered frames to
pre-0163 -- Surface::loadImage's cache lookup miss-of-empty-cache
falls through to plain SDL_LoadBMP, no preload runs (init()
sentinel-checks enabled() and returns). The build-qa byte-identity
gate verifies this property against the v2 binary (c8dd7737) via
the W92-DEF-style A/B (CACHE-OFF rendered frames == pre-0163 rendered
frames).

CACHE-ON path: tested in the iter against the freeze-elimination
acceptance criterion (PLAY1 max inter_flip < 250 ms AND operator-
perceptual "freezes are gone", AND'd).

Single-lever-per-binary: the cache is THE operator-visible
mechanism this binary introduces. SDL-side patches (0066/0067/0068)
are unchanged ride-alongs from prior binaries.

Files in this patch:
- src/nxe_cache.{cpp,h} -- new TU; sibling module to ResourceManager
  (singleton boundary kept clean), ~280 LOC total.
- src/graphics/Surface.cpp -- loadImage intercept B at SDL_LoadBMP.
- src/main.cpp -- nxe::cache::init() call site + #include
  "nxe_cache.h".

(v1 included src/nxe_fmemopen.{cpp,h} + src/common/misc.h myfopen
edit; v2 drops both -- DJGPP libc has neither funopen nor
fmemopen, and the SDL_LoadBMP_IO route covers the dominant freeze
cause without a libc workaround.)

CMake picks up the new top-level src/*.cpp files automatically via
the existing file(GLOB) -- no CMakeLists.txt change needed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>
